WEBVTT

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.120
<i>It's hot.</i>

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.800
<i>It's true that it's hard on the drivers,</i>

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.460
<i>but with this heat, it's also hard on the machine.</i>

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.380
<i>Engine...  Tires...  Brakes...</i>

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.620
<i>Engine...  Tires...  Brakes...</i>

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.110
<i>Engine...  Tires...  Brakes...</i>

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.540
<i>Their temperature becomes extremely high.</i>

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.430
<i>It's because they're already hot that the extra heat becomes a burden.</i>

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:29.390
<i>That's right.</i>

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:34.440
<i>From here on it'll be a battle of how good you care for your machine and lead it to the goal.</i>

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.550
<i>He may not be able to survive just by speed.</i>

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.660
<i>There's something wrong with the sound of the engine!</i>

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:47.450
<i>Capeta's?</i>

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.510
<i>Taira!</i>

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.040
<i>Is there anything wrong with the water temperature?!</i>

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:54.470
<i>Hey.  Answer me.</i>

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:55.580
<i>Taira!</i>

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.520
<i>Can't you hear me?!</i>

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.170
<i>Taira!</i>

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.220
<i>I know...</i>

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.480
<i>that the pressure and water temperature are rising...</i>

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:23.780
<i>and that at this rate the engine and gear will burn out.</i>

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.530
<i>But...</i>

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:50.890
<i>I can't go back to the pit when I've come this far!</i>

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.700
<b>Taira's finally within attacking range!</b>

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:59.570
<b>Shiba and Taira... only 0.5 seconds between them!</b>

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:08.880
<i>If I go in the pit now...</i>

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.700
<i>my race is over.</i>

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.740
<i>Just a bit more...</i>

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.450
<i>I've finally come this close to the top, close enough to grasp it in my hands!</i>

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.720
<i>Please...</i>

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.590
<i>I know it's tough, but just a bit longer...</i>

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.360
<i>Run...</i>

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.550
<i>Run until the end!</i>

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:45.980
<b>Now the top three are entering the 13th lap like triplets with hardly any gap between them.</b>

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.370
Capeta-niichan!

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.110
All right, Capeta!

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.110
Go!  Go!  Go!

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.860
Go for it!

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:51.860
Full speed!

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.000
Capeta!

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:55.080
Go!  Go!

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.080
Capeta!

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.710
The radio should be working.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.920
We may be able to fix it if we can clean the radiator like in the qualifier.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.460
Just 3 more laps.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.930
If he's lucky, it may hold until the end of the race.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.640
But that's a gamble!

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:18.830
That's right.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.680
But that's what he chose to do.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:24.180
Rather than finishing this race securely...

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.650
he chose to win!

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:30.690
Luck is also important to have as a racing driver.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:36.520
In order for Taira to aim higher, he has to put strong luck on his side.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:43.630
To find out if he has that in him,
 this race will be a major touchstone for Taira.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:50.880
<i>The brake!</i>

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.230
Capeta!

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:37.970
That sure was close...

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:39.040
Capeta-niichan!

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.450
Do your best!

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:42.680
I thought he'd go off the course again.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.470
His brakes are coming loose.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.520
Coming loose?

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:51.730
The brake discs aren't working anymore because of the heat, no matter how hard he steps on them.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:53.620
Th-That means...

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:55.190
That's dangerous!

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.950
It's not a matter of dangerous.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:58.920
One mistake and he'll have an accident!

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:01.950
Kid...

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.910
No way...  Why?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.170
For each corner, he did full braking...

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:11.600
and continuing to drive like this, turning by force,

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:14.280
it's obvious there was a heavy burden on the brakes.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.970
When he desperately found a driving style...

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:19.640
To think that it was damaging the machine as well.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:27.270
<i>Please!</i>

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.380
<i>Let him drive until the very end!</i>

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.810
<i>Win no matter what, Ca-chan!</i>

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:38.570
<i>Don't give up until the very end!</i>

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.350
Huh?

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.690
Don't you think Capeta's turning the corners incredibly well?

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:56.670
He's drifting!

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:57.050
Huh?

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:58.440
That's right.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.270
Four-wheel drifting.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:02.130
The driving technique which a renowned F1 driver,

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:07.020
Sideways Ronnie or Ronnie Peterson, specialized in.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:12.350
He lets the tires drift on purpose, and the moment the body of the car faces the exit of the turn,

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.260
he steps on the accelerator.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:19.360
By doing so, the machine drives around the corner without losing any speed.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.550
Très bien!

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:36.300
<i>Taira!</i>

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:40.260
<i>I won't let you get in front of me, no matter what!</i>

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.080
<i>I won't give up!</i>

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:45.220
<i>I'm going in front!</i>

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:56.120
<b>Whoa!  Taira makes a move here!</b>

00:06:58.280 --> 00:06:59.740
<i>I'm not letting you go!</i>

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:02.160
<b>Shiba isn't giving in either!</b>

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:04.960
<b>This is a clash between pride and pride!</b>

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.550
Capeta!

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:17.260
Ryou!

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:19.060
W-Who's in front?!

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:20.100
Is it Capeta?!

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.220
Capeta-kun!

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:35.890
He did it!

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:36.690
But...!

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:38.870
<b>Taira and Shiba are neck and neck!</b>

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:41.380
<b>Plus they're shortening their gap with Ishihara!</b>

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:43.660
<b>The three cars are almost in a ball!</b>

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:47.360
Let's get Ryou to block so Ishihara gets away.

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:49.740
Kagami-san!

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.770
It's just 2 more laps.

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:51.660
Huh?

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:56.330
Let's see this through without splashing cold water on them.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.840
Yup, yup.  Yup, yup!

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:00.870
<b>Ishihara enters the 14th lap in top place!</b>

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:03.000
<b>But Shiba and Taira are closing in on him!</b>

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:06.800
<b>Clearly the two behind him have more power!</b>

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:07.660
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:08.770
<i>I can't get them off!</i>

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:09.670
<i>I can do it!</i>

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:10.980
<i>If I pass him, I'll be at the top!</i>

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:12.690
<i>Go!</i>

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.150
Go!

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:20.430
Capeta!

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.610
Capeta-niichan!

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:23.880
Capeta!

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:25.580
Capeta-kun!

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:27.320
Ryou!

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:29.200
Capeta!

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.250
All right!

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:59.300
You're at the top, Ryou!

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.770
Capeta-niichan!

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:39.270
Hang in there!

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:42.150
<b>It's the final lap!</b>

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:43.730
<b>Can Shiba get away with it?!</b>

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:46.140
<b>Or will Taira pass him?!</b>

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:49.030
<b>Or will veteran Ishihara show his pride?!</b>

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:55.000
<b>We can't take our eyes off, and the final battle begins!</b>

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:52.260
<b>Now we're at the final corner of the final lap!</b>

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:54.740
<b>This is the last battle!</b>

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:11.840
<b>They're here!</b>

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:13.120
<b>Taira's in the lead!</b>

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:16.620
<b>Holding Shiba back on the final corner, Taira is slightly in the lead!</b>

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:18.080
He did it!  He did it!

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:19.670
All right!

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.540
Go for it!

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.640
All right, Taira!

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:24.540
Taira!

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:26.800
Ryou!

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:28.270
<b>Persec, Taira!</b>

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:32.260
<b>If he makes it to the finish line, it's his first win in his debut race!</b>

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.410
All right!

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.220
We got the lead!

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:40.630
All right, Capeta!

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:16.890
All right!

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.650
<b>Oh no!  It's an engine blow!</b>

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:30.000
<b>Taira's engine blows right before the finish line!</b>

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.110
<b>He's slowing down!</b>

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:36.120
<b>Does Shiba have a chance to win the race now?!</b>

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.880
<b>How can this happen?!</b>

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:50.770
<b>Taira's engine blows right before the finish line!</b>

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.940
<b>He's slowing down!</b>

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:56.260
<b>Does Shiba have a chance to win the race now?!</b>

00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:59.680
<b>Shiba catches up!</b>

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:19.830
<b>The winner is Taira!</b>

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:23.040
<b>Barely holding Shiba back, he takes the win!</b>

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:24.750
All right!

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:31.700
<b>Following Minamoto Naomi, he's won in his first Formula Stellar race!</b>

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.590
<b>It's Taira Capeta's win!</b>

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:39.090
He won.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:40.550
He won!

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:43.060
Ca-chan won!

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:50.170
Are you all right, Capeta?!

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:51.500
Capeta!

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:56.860
Hey, Capeta.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.150
I'm sorry.

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:00.820
I broke the car.

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:01.850
You idiot.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:03.500
You did great.  That sure was something.

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:05.530
You won!

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:07.360
You're amazing!

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:23.430
That was excellent, Ca-chan.  You did great!

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:26.470
To think he'd really win the race!

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:29.950
It's a miracle!  Capeta's done another miracle, Shige-san!

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:31.600
Nope, he was lucky.

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:32.940
Lucky?

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:36.550
No one could tell when the engine would break.

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:41.660
Capeta was able to bring it to the goal because he had strong luck.

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:46.860
With hard work, he's made the impossible a reality so many times.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:49.370
But races aren't won on that alone.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:54.630
At the very edge of battle, it's strong luck that decides everything at the end.

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:57.330
Capeta has that.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:01.090
Luck and hard work.  Capeta's strong at both of them.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:15.650
I thought you and Minamoto were bumps above my eye, but I'm grateful to you both now.

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:20.070
I'll probably be able to have more thrilling races.

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:21.860
I won't lose next time!

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:23.080
Yeah.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:23.820
I won't either.

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.760
That's great, Ryou!

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:28.790
You did great!

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:32.040
Just you watch, Taira Capeta.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:36.750
It went just about as planned, don't you think?

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:39.590
There are times when they grow better in devastated lands.

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:41.720
Taira is growing well.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:46.490
More and more of this generation will be going out into the world.

00:15:46.490 --> 00:15:50.430
With them, I'm sure the world of motor sports will change.

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:51.720
That's right.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.110
It's going to be more fun.

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:59.050
With this, Minamoto's reign is over.

00:15:59.050 --> 00:15:59.570
Huh?

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:04.060
Ca-chan must feel relieved, now that he's beaten him.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:04.920
No.

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:06.160
Minamoto didn't compete.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:07.390
Huh?

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:08.160
What?!

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:12.400
Apparently he suddenly got a call for a Formula Euro test, and he went to Italy—

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:13.630
What did you say?!

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:16.640
If Minamoto's not here, it's obvious he'll win!

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:15.850
Ow ow ow!

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:18.630
I got emotional for no reason!

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:36.240
Komazawa sure is late.

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:40.750
Capeta suddenly took the win in his debut race after all.

00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:45.990
He may not look it, but Komazawa is sensitive at times.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.450
Yo.

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:54.710
Komazawa!

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:54.710
Komazawa-san!

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:55.990
W-What is it?

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.150
You guys are creeping me out.

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:59.300
We were worried that you might not be coming again.

00:16:59.300 --> 00:16:59.910
Hey!

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:02.750
You guys thought I was growing timid, didn't you!

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:03.560
Listen up!

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:06.730
Don't get over your head because you won a race!

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:06.730
Komazawa-san!

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:12.430
Until the 7th race, I'm gonna drive, drive, and drive like hell, and I'll win!  Got it?!

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:14.010
I'm suffocating!

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:14.010
Hey, you guys!

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:18.670
How much do you think it's costing us to borrow this place for half a day?!

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:21.400
Stop yapping and get driving!

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:22.900
Yes sir!

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.100
They're both looking good.

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:39.140
Both Komazawa and Capeta are getting more stable.

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:39.590
Yeah.

00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:42.550
We can look forward to the next race.

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:50.050
<b>I would like to try the B settings next.</b>

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:51.200
Okay.

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:55.700
<i>I got accepted.</i>

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:59.020
<i>In September I'm going to transfer to a British high school.</i>

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:03.300
<i>England is the center of motor sports.</i>

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:08.990
<i>In the first half of the year, I'll learn English and start studying seriously...</i>

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:13.340
<i>so that I can be a racing manager who won't embarrass you.</i>

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:14.350
<i>Nobu.</i>

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:17.020
<i>The kart and FSte are both connected to the world.</i>

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:21.130
<i>So if you carry on winning, the F1 isn't a dream!</i>

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:28.440
<i>Continue rising, Capeta!</i>

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:31.560
<i>Continue driving up to the top!</i>

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:35.680
<i>Wherever you go, I'll follow you always!</i>

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:39.770
<i>I want to race with you again!</i>

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:42.350
<i>I'll catch up to you no matter what!</i>

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:25.070
Minamoto.

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:28.430
I heard you went to Italy.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:29.450
Yeah.

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:32.080
I signed a contract with a team over there.

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:36.740
I heard you won your debut race.

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:38.190
Yeah.

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:46.720
In two weeks' time, I'm also going to have a debut race over there.

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:49.670
Once I leave Japan, I won't be coming back for a while.

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:30.310
<b><i>itsukara ka gomakashi kirenu hodo ni hibiiteiru</i></b>

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:30.310
<b><i>For some time it's been ringing out; it can't be hidden anymore</i></b>

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:36.000
<b><i>hirameki to iu na no oto wo</i></b>

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:36.000
<b><i>A sound called insight</i></b>

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:41.420
<b><i>koko de narashiteiru no sa</i></b>

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:41.420
<b><i>It's ringing here</i></b>

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:47.060
<b><i>kokoro ga furueru</i></b>

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:47.060
<b><i>My heart is trembling</i></b>

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:52.490
